# Negative control: REAL furniture, verbatim from the `flutter test --coverage`
# transcript of CI run 35478132251's `Coverage / Flutter Coverage` job — the
# capture that job scans with `--rules-only`. What the JOB LOG adds is undone —
# its job/step/timestamp column stripped, its `##[group]`/`##[endgroup]` put
# back to the `::group::`/`::endgroup::` the reporter writes to the tee'd file.
#
# This is the SAME sink class as `furniture.flutter-test.log` and a DIFFERENT
# reporter. `flutter test` picks its reporter from the environment
# (`test_core`'s `defaultReporter` in `runner/configuration/reporters.dart`:
# `GITHUB_ACTIONS == 'true'` wins over `compact`), so on a hosted runner there
# is NO `HH:MM +N:` progress line anywhere in the transcript — the older fixture
# is a local capture and carries only the compact one. Run 35478132251 was rc 4
# on exactly that: every test passed, and the `drive` class's proof-of-run
# pattern matched none of the transcript. These lines are what it must match:
#   * `✅ <path>: <name>` — a test that finished, one line, no output;
#   * `::group::✅ …` / `::endgroup::` — the same, wrapping the output the test
#     printed, which is where every app line of a github-reporter transcript is;
#   * `::group::❎ … (skipped)` — a test whose BODY never ran, which is why the
#     skip glyph is deliberately NOT proof of a run.
# The closing `🎉` summary is furniture too, and is not the proof either: the
# reporter writes it whatever the counts are, `0 tests passed` included.

